/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (I am an Aerospace Engineering graduate from the University of Bristol. As I was born in the US and raised in Mexico before moving to the UK for my degree, therefore I bring a global perspective to engineering, one shaped by adapting across three countries and collaborating with people from very different backgrounds.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (My academic strengths lie in Aerospace Vehicle Design and Systems Integration \(AVDASI\), Space Systems, and Advanced Materials, and my work spans CFD, structural simulation, hands-on manufacturing, and electronics. My current research project is a parametric aerodynamic study of an F1 front wing, pairing STAR-CCM+ simulations with a MATLAB surrogate model to map performance across the full design space. Alongside this, I have designed and manufactured a UAV for wind-tunnel testing and contributed to a water filtration project for a community in Cambodia. These are experiences that have taught me to engineer for both performance and people.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (Outside the classroom, I am an active member of Bristol SEDS, where I have contributed to the design of the rocket feed system, valve actuation, and hot-fire simulation modelling.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
